  "content": {
    "id": "p32-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "How many ways can you arrange the letters in the word GREAT so that the resulting string:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p32-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "begins with a vowel",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$48$",
          "worked": "There are two vowels, A and E. Choose the first letter, then arrange the remaining four letters.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Number of arrangements}&=2\\times4!\\\\\\text{Number of arrangements}&=48\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "ends with a vowel",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$48$",
          "worked": "Choose the last letter from A and E, then arrange the remaining four letters.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Number of arrangements}&=2\\times4!\\\\\\text{Number of arrangements}&=48\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "begins and ends with a vowel",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$12$",
          "worked": "There are two choices for the first vowel and one for the last. Arrange G, R and T in the three middle positions.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Number of arrangements}&=2\\times1\\times3!\\\\\\text{Number of arrangements}&=12\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "begins or ends with a vowel?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$84$\n\nAdd the two end-condition counts and subtract arrangements with vowels at both ends.",
          "worked": "Let $A$ be the set of arrangements beginning with a vowel and $B$ the set ending with a vowel. From parts (a)–(c), $|A|=48$, $|B|=48$ and $|A\\cap B|=12$.\n$$\\begin{align*}|A\\cup B|&=|A|+|B|-|A\\cap B|\\\\|A\\cup B|&=48+48-12\\\\|A\\cup B|&=84\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
  },
